Compute the required amount without mutating state: `uint256 requiredBalance = totals[token].elastic + fee;` then check `_tokenBalanceOf(token) >= requiredBalance` and only THEN update totals. Alternatively add a reentrancy guard. The addElastic call should be separated from the require check:

uint256 newElastic = totals[token].elastic + fee;
require(_tokenBalanceOf(token) >= newElastic, 'BentoBox: Wrong amount');
totals[token].elastic = newElastic.to128();

Same fix as flashLoan: separate the elastic update from the check. Additionally, track fees per token in a mapping to handle duplicates correctly:

mapping(IERC20 => uint256) memory tokenFees; // accumulate fees per token
for (uint256 i = 0; i < len; i++) {
    tokenFees[tokens[i]] += fees[i];
}
for each unique token: require balance >= totals[token].elastic + tokenFees[token]);
for each unique token: totals[token].addElastic(tokenFees[token]);

